  "$schema": "../registry.schema.json",
  "id": "ais-live-v2",
  "name": "AIS LIVE v2",
  "number": "11",
  "status": "draft",
  "inspiration": "Evolution of 03-ais-live (the command-deck broadcast look) built for the October VSL wave. Same DNA: onyx canvas, perspective-grid tunnel, conic beam, chrome/blue italic-900 type, whip cuts. New: a shared stroke-icon vocabulary drawn on via pathLength, liquid-glass chips with sheen sweeps, and story-telling diagram cards (ladder, versus, growth-lines, hub, timeline) so beats show ideas instead of only setting type. Headline slots support <br> line control and <em> phrases never split across lines.",
  "summary": "High-energy live-event motion graphics with an icon + diagram vocabulary. Use when a beat should TELL the story (departments as icon rows, tools-vs-system as a duel, growth as a chart, the AI OS as a hub) rather than restate the line as text.",
  "palette": {
    "bg": "#07121C",
    "fg": "#FFFFFF",
    "accent": "#37BDF8",
    "accent2": "#FF8A5C",
    "alert": "#FF3B30",
    "notes": "All-blue accent directive: every accent, icon, label and gradient is AIS blue; coral survives only as an ambient bg glow; red is the LIVE dot only. AIS/LIVE mark stays solid."
  },
  "fonts": {
    "display": "Montserrat",
    "body": "Inter",
    "mono": "JetBrains Mono",
    "notes": "Montserrat italic-900 headlines/numbers/mark; Inter body/subs; JetBrains Mono eyebrows/labels/units. No serif."
  },
  "motion": "Word-by-word blur+rise headlines (expo.out); glass icon chips pop (back.out 1.7) with stroke draw-on (pathLength 100 -> dashoffset 0) and a specular sheen sweep; diagram connectors draw with power2.inOut; count-ups pop with a charging tick meter. Ambient rides the BACKGROUND ONLY (tunnel push-in, beam rock, sparkle crosshairs, breathing vignette); the text layer never scales or translates. Deterministic. Cards are SELF-SCOPING (dash comp-ids, #id-prefixed CSS, ROOT-scoped queries) so inline assembly needs no script rewriting.",
  "transitions": "Master-timeline motion-blur whips between beats (build-side), never hard cuts. No in-card light streaks (retired by directive 8/31).",
